Unreleased
    Repair calls are capped per run with --repair-limit (default: one
    release worth of attempts) and never run concurrently, so a repair
    agent cannot be started more often than the user allowed.
    install accepts --jobs K (or install.jobs in the config) to build
    independent releases in parallel. Receipts record phase start and finish
    times.
    Rebuild from clean sources after an external repair, so make programs
    with one-second timestamps cannot test stale build products.
    Tests compare canonical paths and pass on macOS.
    Receipts record the platform: operating system, architecture name,
    compiler, make program, thread support, and XPerl commit.
    Add install-ported, which rebuilds every release recorded as successful
    in the ports registry with a dry run, filters, resumable state, and
    JSON and text reports.

0.002  2026-11-06
    Add TOML configuration and named external repair agent profiles.

0.001  2026-11-06
    Initial standalone XPerl installer distribution.
